"blunder","great","best","great","best","great","best","blunder","best","best","best","best","best","best"],"moments":[{"ply":39,"name":"20.Nxd5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"20.Nxd5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the knight on d5.","Protects the bishop on f4, which was hanging.","The next best move, 20.Bxc4, would drop White's winning chances from 59% to 43% (−0.80).","20.Nxd5 stops …Na3+.","Black was threatening …Na3+, winning a bishop for a rook, picking it up with 21…Nxf4. Nxd5 takes care of it.","Trades knights."]},{"ply":55,"name":"28.Rxc4","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"28.Rxc4!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the rook on c4 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 28…Bxc4 29.Rxc4 Rxc4 30.Bxc4 the engine rates it +0.84.","Takes the pawn on c4.","28.Rxc4 trades off the attacked rook instead of losing it to …Bxf4.","Black was threatening …Bxf4, winning the exchange. The rook takes something with it instead.","Takes the c4 pawn."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"28.Rxc4!! offers the rook on c4. Taking it gives White the material back and more."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"28.Rxc4 puts the rook on c4 where it can be taken by the bishop on d5 and the rook on c8. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the rook","text":"28…Bxc4 is met by 29.Bxc4, taking the bishop on c4 and threatening Bxa6, winning the exchange. Then 31.bxc3 takes the rook on c3, and 32.Rc4 threatens Rc7+, joining the attack on the king. White ends up a pawn ahead: White is a little better (+0.68). This is Black's best try."}]},{"ply":64,"name":"32…Bd2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"32…Bd2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked bishop to safety.","The next best move, 32…Bg5, would drop Black's winning chances from 63% to 52% (−0.21).","32…Bd2 threatens …Bxc3, winni