d pawn to c6, close to promotion.","Takes d7 away from the rook on d8.","The next best move, 70.Ba6, would drop White's winning chances from 48% to 36% (−1.54).","70.c6 pushes the passed pawn to c6.","Black answers 70…Rf8.","After 70…Rf8 71.c7 Kd6 72.Ba6 Kc6 73.c8=R+ Rxc8 74.Bxc8 Kxb6 75.Bxe6 a4, the pawn promotes on c8, the rooks are traded and White comes out a piece and a pawn up (−0.02)."]},{"ply":141,"name":"71.c7","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"71.c7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to c7, close to promotion.","Attacks the rook on d8, which is undefended.","The next best move, 71.Ke2, would drop White's winning chances from 49% to 29% (−2.40).","71.c7 threatens cxd8=Q+, winning a rook.","It threatens cxd8=Q+, winning a rook, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black answers 71…Rg8."]}],"opening":{"name":"Sicilian Defense: Najdorf Variation","eco":"B95","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9…Qc7: 18 moves in all, 9 by White and 9 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9…Qc7: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}